# PLAN CLI SKEPTICS — three independent checkers

File: openOODA/audit/plan_cli_skeptics.oot
Run after all three phalanxes report INT green, or after a ship
asks for an early reject. Skeptics do not write product code.
They may write only their audit notes.

Smoke is a suspect. A test that would pass if the defect remained
is not proof (WORKFLOW section 3).

## 1. SK1 — Lie detector

  Question: would this test still pass if we reverted the ship?

  Ship 1
    If the smoke only greps `completionProvider` in cli/*.oo
    source, fail. Drive the rebuilt bin/ooda over stdio.
    If initialize lacks completionProvider, fail.
    If `&Fs` at a real cursor does not yield `&FsCap`, fail.
    Re-run lsp_cursor_smoke. If hover is first-fn-only, fail.

  Ship 2
    If --exec still runs `test -e`, fail.
    strings on bin/ooda must not be the only proof.
    Run the exec fixture. Require LAUNCH_EXEC_OK in output.
    Revert-test: a binary that only checks exists must fail SK1.
    Without --exec, LAUNCH_EXEC_OK must be absent.

  Ship 3
    If output is still `ooda bench: ok`, fail.
    If the smoke greps `now_ms` in source and does not run
    `ooda bench fixtures/hello.oo`, fail.
    Missing file must not exit 0.

  Double-run every CRIT in a new shell.

## 2. SK2 — Exec and capability

  Question: did we add a new shell or a wider token?

  Refuse
    New `sh -c` around user payload (ship 2).
    `date` / bash timers (ship 3).
    SysCap used where TimeCap is enough (ship 3).
    Completion that process_execs oodac for each keystroke
    unless COORD named that design (ship 1 must not).

  Check
    launch --exec uses run_oodac_run / find_oodac.
    Gate still runs before the child.
    Hostile yank / sha / caps still non-zero.
    File URIs in lsp do not walk `..` to /etc.

  Product tokens
    Give only the token the function needs (RULES 1.4).
    Record the main signature for ship 3.

## 3. SK3 — Isolation and collision

  Question: did we touch the locked trees or the dirty main worktree?

  Must be clean
    No diff in oodac/, runtime/, std/, ooda/std/.
    No edit of openOODA.github.io (owner likes the page).
    No edit of the dirty `/home/jeryd/Projects/openOODA/ooda`
    working tree. Worktrees only.
    oodac/oodac mtime in the parent tree is unchanged.
    No new `.py` / `.md` / `.sh`.
    No file over 256 lines.
    vscode/ and ooda/lsp/ not grown.

  Merge gate
    SK1, SK2, SK3 each write audit/plan_skN.oot.
    Status is PASS or FAIL with the command that proved it.
    COORD may merge a ship only if that ship is PASS on all three.
    Parent (this agent) re-runs any CRIT before telling the owner
    the ship is done. Do not trust a skeptic that only read code.

## 4. Swarm counts

  Per ship: 12 agents (COORD DE1 DE2 RT PV1 PV2 SEC MEM INT HARN HYG DOCS).
  Across three ships: 36.
  Plus 3 skeptics: 39 children.
  Live cap: host queues above 32. Launch one ship phalanx at a
  time if the host refuses the panel, or launch Wave 0 of all
  three, then Wave 1 of all three.

  Stuck: kill the child. Do not assign two agents to the same
  debug. File isolation is mandatory.

## 5. What the owner sees

  After skeptics:
    Ship 1: completion on `ooda lsp` — pass/fail + command.
    Ship 2: launch --exec runs — pass/fail + command.
    Ship 3: bench prints ms — pass/fail + command.
    What is not done: site, oodac, std, install, fuzz.
